AuronQ Universal Miner v0.4.6-alpha release trigger

Broad NVIDIA + cross-vendor GPU update:
- keeps current CUDA 13.2 backend for modern/new NVIDIA targets
- packages CUDA 12.6 compatibility backend for supported Maxwell/Pascal/Volta
- packages CUDA 11.8 compatibility backend for supported Kepler sm_35/sm_37
- GTX 10xx/Pascal can use native CUDA 12.x compatibility path when canonical AQM64 self-test passes
- AMD/Intel/NVIDIA generic fallback remains OpenCL
- Solo AUTO: current CUDA -> CUDA 12.x legacy -> CUDA 11.8 Kepler -> OpenCL GPU -> CPU
- Pool mode no longer rejects older NVIDIA GPUs using AuronQ native CUDA eligibility
- GUI shows actual AUTO fallback reason
- no dedicated ASIC integration
- no Mainnet consensus changes
